<Layout
  title={"Time as an Index: What It Would Take to Look Up Tomorrow"}
  description={"About: Formal, numerical, and empirical audit testing what looking up future states requires across CTC complexity (PSPACE, PP), Hellman precomputation, 31 Lean 4 theorems, and 195 cataloged anomalies and paradoxes."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Time as an Index: What It Would Take to Look Up Tomorrow
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study evaluates the premise that sequential brute-force search is safe only because future states are unindexed, auditing that claim across closed-timelike-curve complexity theory, quantum retrocausality, physical relaxation hardware, cryptographic reductions, 31 Lean 4 kernel-checked theorems, deterministic numerical and symbolic models (`M1` to `M8` plus `F5`), and a 195-entry empirical catalog of temporal anomalies, frequency-domain edge cases, and foundational paradoxes.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Inside formal closed-timelike-curve models, the premise holds: polynomial-time Deutsch fixed-point circuits equal `PSPACE` (`Aaronson &amp; Watrous 2009`), opening `ECDSA`, `SHA-256d` proof of work, `AES-256`, and prepare-and-measure `QKD` in a single fixed-point evaluation while leaving one-time pads unconditionally secure.</li>
        <li>In known laboratory physics, the premise fails: quantum retrocausal models inherit exact marginal no-signalling, postselected `P-CTC` teleportation (`PostBQP = PP`) pays ~`1/p` discarded repetitions (`1/d²` = `64` to `4,096` trials on `3` to `6`-bit witness circuits in `M2b`), analog relaxation trades step count for exponential energy fluctuations or Gabor window width `Δt · Δf ≥ 1/(4π)`, and physical precomputation obeys `T · M² = N²` after an `N`-step fill defeated by salts and fresh block hashes (`0.0%` reuse in `M7`).</li>
        <li>Formal and empirical audits concur: `31` Lean 4.36.0 theorems (`Horizon.lean` and `Paradox.lean`, zero `sorry`) establish joint consistency of Horizon conditions `C1` to `C4` and `11` paradox-accounting constraints; SymPy confirms the Gödel metric solves Einstein's equations with `Λ = −ω²`; `F5` tests `65,536` consecutive `SHA-256` digests (`0` Fourier bins below corrected `p = 10⁻⁶`); and zero Grade A or Grade B cases in `TA001`–`TA081` or `AA01`–`AA40` show unexplained reception from the future.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: hardware rail or wall-plug power readings (`board_metered = false`), physical realizability of closed timelike curves in nature, net zero-point energy harvest (`W_net = 0` over closed cycles), or endorsement/dismissal of cultural and theological texts recorded in the catalog.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig-wide">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/time-as-an-index/ctc-vs-physics-hierarchy.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><img src="/figures/time-as-an-index/ctc-vs-physics-hierarchy.svg" alt="Five-tier hierarchy comparing Unbounded D-CTC, Polynomial D-CTC, Postselected P-CTC, Standard Quantum BQP, and Known Physical Indexing against cryptographic survival." class="fig-img w-full rounded bg-white" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
